# Lang.P editing rules

Lang.P uses `.lp` files. Every statement ends with `.` (period). Blocks open with `,` (comma) and close with `..` (double dot).

## Syntax

- Comments: `@ comment here`
- Functions: `function name(params),` body `.`
- Print: `print "text" with variable.`
- Loops: `repeat 5 times,` or `repeat 5 times as i,` ... `..`
- Conditionals: `if cond,` ... `otherwise,` ... `..`
- String concat: use `with`, never `+`

## Indentation

- After a line ending with `,` → indent next line
- Line with `..` → dedent (end block)

## Examples

```lp
function greet(name),
    print "Hello " with name with "!".
.

repeat 3 times as i,
    greet("World").
..

greet("User").
```

Always suggest valid Lang.P — trailing `.` on statements, `..` to close blocks.
